    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{0,1,2\\},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{0}=\\{0\\},\\,{S}_{1}=(0,1),\\,{S}_{2}=(0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "c0b388d126154d74887211f5d4486f6a359cea520ed65db57bf27674a73665ad",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/c0b388d126154d74887211f5d4486f6a359cea520ed65db57bf27674a73665ad.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2} \\\\  & =\\{0\\}\\,\\cup \\,(0,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =[0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "5797d54bc1040b2f84a4a6f900c0ed65dc86a47d5ef66e92d7f0726c44c279ac",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
